<p class="mh-legal-lead">Artificial intelligence should help people grow—not replace human judgment.</p>
<p class="mh-legal-lead">Responsible AI is fundamental to how we design, build, and continuously improve the MedhaIQ platform.</p>
<p class="mh-legal-lead">At MedhaIQ, AI is designed to provide structured coaching, objective feedback, and career insights that help professionals prepare more effectively for interviews and career transitions. Our systems are built to support learning and continuous improvement, not to make hiring decisions or determine employment outcomes.</p>
<p class="mh-legal-lead">Below, we explain how we design, use, and govern AI across the MedhaIQ platform.</p>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="ai-philosophy">
  <h2>01. Our AI Philosophy</h2>
  <p>We believe AI should empower people—not evaluate their worth.</p>
  <p>MedhaIQ uses artificial intelligence to simulate interviews, analyze communication, identify strengths and improvement areas, and generate personalized coaching recommendations. Our AI is designed to help you become better prepared—not to replace recruiters, hiring managers, or professional judgment.</p>
  <p>Every feature we build is guided by five core principles:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Human-First Coaching</li>
    <li>Transparency</li>
    <li>Privacy by Design</li>
    <li>Human Oversight</li>
    <li>Continuous Improvement</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="supports-learning">
  <h2>02. AI Supports Learning, Not Hiring</h2>
  <p>MedhaIQ is not a recruitment platform.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not make hiring decisions.</li>
    <li>We do not rank candidates for employers.</li>
    <li>We do not determine employability.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>AI-generated interview scores are intended solely to help you understand your preparation level, identify opportunities for improvement, and track progress over time. Employment decisions remain the sole responsibility of human employers.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="how-ai-evaluates">
  <h2>03. How AI Evaluates Responses</h2>
  <p>Our AI is designed to evaluate the quality of interview responses—not the individual. Depending on the interview type and available context, MedhaIQ may evaluate characteristics of the response such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Clarity of communication</li>
    <li>Logical structure and completeness of responses</li>
    <li>Relevance to the question</li>
    <li>Behavioral storytelling and STAR methodology usage</li>
    <li>Technical reasoning, leadership, and decision-making examples</li>
    <li>Professional tone and delivery</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Scores are generated using structured evaluation frameworks aligned with interview best practices rather than subjective opinions.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="what-ai-does-not-evaluate">
  <h2>04. What AI Does NOT Evaluate</h2>
  <p>MedhaIQ is designed to evaluate the quality of interview responses rather than personal characteristics such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Age</li>
    <li>Gender</li>
    <li>Race or ethnicity</li>
    <li>Religion or political beliefs</li>
    <li>Nationality</li>
    <li>Disability</li>
    <li>Personal or group identity</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where voice or video capabilities are available, MedhaIQ is designed to evaluate communication effectiveness and response quality rather than demographic characteristics or personal identity.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="human-judgment">
  <h2>05. Human Judgment Always Matters</h2>
  <p>AI is an assistant—not an authority.</p>
  <p>While our models generate personalized insights and recommendations, they should be viewed as coaching guidance rather than absolute truth. AI-generated feedback may occasionally contain inaccuracies, omissions, or interpretations that differ from those of human interviewers. Users should apply their own judgment when interpreting recommendations.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="transparency">
  <h2>06. Transparency</h2>
  <p>We believe users should always understand when and how AI is being used.</p>
  <p>Whenever MedhaIQ generates interview questions, scores, summaries, or coaching recommendations, those outputs are created using artificial intelligence. We do not present AI-generated content as if it were produced by a human reviewer.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="privacy-trust">
  <h2>07. Privacy &amp; Trust</h2>
  <p>Privacy is foundational to trust.</p>
  <p>Interview sessions, resumes, transcripts, reports, and evaluation history remain private to your account unless you choose to share them or disclosure is required by applicable law. We never sell your personal information to advertisers. We configure our infrastructure and AI providers to protect customer information wherever supported by their services and contractual commitments.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="ai-models-partners">
  <h2>08. AI Models &amp; Technology Partners</h2>
  <p>MedhaIQ integrates trusted AI technologies to power interview simulations, coaching insights, transcription, speech synthesis, and other platform capabilities. We select providers based on rigorous criteria:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Security &amp; compliance</li>
    <li>Reliability &amp; performance</li>
    <li>Privacy commitments</li>
    <li>Model quality &amp; safety boundaries</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Our modular architecture allows us to evolve underlying AI models over time while maintaining strict adherence to our privacy and governance standards. We periodically review the AI services we use to ensure they continue to meet our standards for privacy, reliability, and responsible deployment.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="your-data-controls">
  <h2>09. Your Data &amp; Controls</h2>
  <p>You remain in complete control of your information. At any time, you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access your interview history</li>
    <li>Review and export generated reports</li>
    <li>Manage account preferences</li>
    <li>Request complete deletion of your personal data in accordance with our Privacy Policy</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="human-oversight">
  <h2>10. Human Oversight &amp; User Agency</h2>
  <p>Artificial intelligence is designed to support—not replace—human judgment.</p>
  <p>You remain in control of how you use the insights generated by MedhaIQ. AI-generated feedback is intended to help you prepare, reflect, and improve, while career decisions, interview strategies, and professional actions remain your responsibility.</p>
  <p>Where appropriate, users are encouraged to combine AI-generated insights with personal experience, professional mentoring, and independent judgment.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="continuous-improvement">
  <h2>11. Continuous Improvement &amp; Model Evolution</h2>
  <p>Artificial intelligence continues to evolve rapidly, and so does MedhaIQ.</p>
  <p>We regularly review and improve our evaluation methodologies, prompts, and AI integrations to enhance consistency, accuracy, and overall user experience. As models and technologies improve, we may update components of our AI systems while remaining committed to the principles outlined in this Responsible AI Policy.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="feedback">
  <h2>12. Feedback &amp; Continuous Learning</h2>
  <p>We welcome feedback on the quality, fairness, and usefulness of AI-generated experiences.</p>
  <p>If you believe an evaluation is inaccurate, misleading, or inconsistent with our principles, we encourage you to contact us.</p>
  <p>User feedback plays an important role in helping us improve our systems, refine our evaluation methodologies, and strengthen the overall MedhaIQ experience.</p>
</section>

<section class="mh-legal-section" id="our-commitment">
  <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
  <p>We believe the best AI doesn't replace human potential—it helps unlock it.</p>
  <p>Our mission is to help professionals prepare with greater confidence, communicate more effectively, and make better-informed career decisions through responsible use of artificial intelligence.</p>
  <p>We are committed to designing AI systems that are transparent, privacy-conscious, and continuously improving, while always keeping people—not algorithms—at the center of the experience.</p>
  <p>We believe responsible AI is an ongoing commitment. As technology evolves, so will our practices, governance, and safeguards—always with the goal of helping professionals grow with confidence, transparency, and trust.</p>
  <p>Every AI capability we build will continue to be guided by the principles of transparency, fairness, privacy, and human empowerment that define MedhaIQ.</p>
</section>
